# Own-wording Transformations of Grim Hollow Player's Guide (2014 rules). TRANS = {name: {intro, stages: {n: {rule, take, fixed, d}}, opt: {name: text}}}.
# The 2014 data lists only the Boons and Flaws, so each Level is one feat. The Level 1 core features of the Transformation are not in the data.
def _intro(n, extra=""):
    return "%s Transformation. It has four Levels and each Level adds Boons and sometimes a Flaw. Your GM decides how you advance.%s" % (n, (" " + extra) if extra else "")
ONE = "Choose one Boon from the list. Boons with a requirement need the earlier Boon named in it. You also gain the Flaw of this Level, if one is listed."
def _fixed(lv):
    return {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": lv}
TRANS = {
"Aberrant Horror": {"intro": _intro("Aberrant Horror"),
 "stages": {2: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Unearthly Senses"]},
            3: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Shifting Form"]},
            4: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level. It needs Shifting Form.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Amorphous Flesh"]}},
 "opt": {
  "Unearthly Senses": "As a bonus action, enhance your sense organs or grow new ones and pick one Adaptation. Keen Senses: Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that use sight, hearing or smell. Darkvision: you see in dim light within 60 ft as bright light and in darkness as dim light, with no color. If you already have darkvision, its range becomes 120 ft. Third Eye: you see invisible creatures and objects as if they were visible. An Adaptation lasts until you fall unconscious, pick another, or end it with a bonus action. At Level 4 you can have two Adaptations at once.",
  "Shifting Form": "Your body loses its cohesion and softens like jelly. You take no extra damage from critical hits. Each attack you make with your Eldritch Limbs deals an extra 1d6 Acid damage. You have Resistance to Acid damage.",
  "Amorphous Flesh": "Your body dissolves into a corrosive slurry. You can squeeze through gaps 1 inch wide and are immune to being Grappled, Prone and Restrained. When you take 10 or more Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing damage, you can split along the wound into two bodies one size smaller, each with half your current hit points (you choose who gets an odd point) and sharing your gear as you choose. On your turn you move and take one action with each body. You have one bonus action and one reaction per turn, used by either body. As an action, either body can reform when the two are within 5 ft. You regain hit points equal to the other body's current hit points and return to normal size. The second body lasts 1 hour before it dissolves."}},
"Fey": {"intro": _intro("Fey", "At Level 1 you pick the Summer or Winter court. Your court changes several later Boons and Flaws."),
 "stages": {1: {"rule": "You gain Fey Form and Twilight Step, and the Planar Binding (Fey) Flaw. Choose your court with Fey Form.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Fey Form", "Twilight Step"]},
            2: {"rule": ONE, "take": 1, "fixed": []}, 3: {"rule": ONE, "take": 1, "fixed": []}, 4: {"rule": ONE, "take": 1, "fixed": []}},
 "opt": {
  "Fey Form": "Your Charisma rises by 2 and Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 16 from this. You become a fey in addition to your other types. Spells that affect humanoids still affect you, but you are immune to effects that only affect fey of a specific CR. Choose the court that fuels your Transformation. The Summer Court stands for warmth and plenty, and its fey tend toward cheer, whim and vanity, often hiding cruelty behind beauty. The Winter Court stands for stillness and dark, and its fey tend toward seriousness and cruelty, but are direct about their aims.",
  "Twilight Step": "As a bonus action, teleport up to 30 ft to an open space you see. By court, right after the step one creature you see within 5 ft takes damage equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1). Summer deals Fire damage. Winter deals Cold damage. You can use it a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum once). A Long Rest restores all uses.",
  "Planar Binding (Fey)": "Your body and soul are tied to a faerie realm. You have Disadvantage on death saves. If you would be killed, your soul returns to a plane the GM picks and you become an NPC there. In the faerie realm that caused your change, this Flaw does nothing.",
  "Magic Tricks": "You learn one illusion or enchantment cantrip. You also choose one 1st-level and one 2nd-level illusion or enchantment spell and can cast each once with no slot. A Short or Long Rest restores them. Charisma is the spellcasting ability. After a Long Rest you can swap either spell for another of the same level and schools.",
  "Sprite Servant": "A fey sprite serves you. It is a Tiny ball of light that cannot be harmed or affected. It has a fly speed of 40 ft and talks to you telepathically within 1 mile, understanding your languages. It can turn invisible at will and otherwise sheds dim light in a 10-ft radius. As a bonus action you can make it shine bright in a 20-ft radius with dim light for another 20 ft.",
  "Two-Faced": "You can change your face into enchanting beauty or horrid ugliness. Each nonfey creature within 30 ft makes a Wisdom save or is affected for 1 minute. Summer: it is Charmed, and the effect ends if you or an ally harms it. Winter: it is Frightened of you, ending when it finishes a turn out of your line of sight. You can use it a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum once). A Long Rest restores all uses.",
  "Queen's Servant": "The court lends you power and you owe tribute. Twice a year, at the winter and summer solstices, you must give your queen a treasure or other significant tribute. If you miss the day, she pulls you into her faerie realm. You stay there for 100 years or until you bargain for your return. The GM decides what counts as fitting tribute, such as magic items, secrets, captured fey criminals or servants.",
  "Courtly Graces": "You gain proficiency in two skills set by your court, or double your Proficiency Bonus if you already have them. If you already have double in one, you gain another +2 on it. Summer: Performance and Persuasion, and you are immune to being Charmed. Winter: Deception and Intimidation, and you are immune to being Frightened.",
  "Faerie Mantle": "As an action, wrap yourself in faerie majesty for 1 minute. You project blinding beauty in a 30-ft aura. Creatures of your choice that start a turn there or enter it make a Charisma save or are Blinded for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of their turns. Long Rest to use again.",
  "Made of Magic": "Your fey change reshapes your body. You have Resistance to damage from spells. When you make a save against a spell, you can use your reaction to gain Advantage on it. Short or Long Rest to use that again.",
  "Bound by Words": "Fey are bound by their promises, and so are you. When you give your word to a humanoid, by a promise, contract or spoken agreement, it is magically enforced. If you fail your part, you lose all your fey Boons until you give an extra tithe to the queen, on top of those from Queen's Servant. You are bound by the letter of an agreement, not its spirit.",
  "Greater Magic Tricks": "Requires Magic Tricks. Choose one enchantment or illusion spell each of 3rd, 4th and 5th level. You can cast each once with no slot. A Long Rest restores them. Charisma is the spellcasting ability. After a Long Rest you can swap any of them for another of the same level and schools.",
  "Misdirection": "Light and magic bend around you. Attack rolls against you have Disadvantage. A hit disrupts this until the end of your next turn. It works only while you are conscious.",
  "Twilight Glamour": "As an action, turn invisible along with what you wear and carry. It ends if you end it, attack or cast a spell. After it ends you cannot use this for 1 minute. It works only while you are conscious.",
  "Seasonally Affected": "Your fey ties bring a weakness. In the summer court you are Vulnerable to Cold damage. In the winter court you are Vulnerable to Fire damage. Resistance to that type becomes normal damage, and immunity becomes resistance. When you take that damage, your hit point maximum drops by the same amount until you finish a Long Rest."}},
"Primordial": {"intro": _intro("Primordial", "A Primordial is a mortal tied to the elements. Your Primordial Affinity and Dual Nature choose its sources."),
 "stages": {1: {"rule": "You gain Elemental Form and Primordial Affinity, and the Planar Binding (Primordial) Flaw.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Elemental Form", "Primordial Affinity"]},
            2: {"rule": ONE, "take": 1, "fixed": []}, 3: {"rule": ONE, "take": 1, "fixed": []}, 4: {"rule": ONE, "take": 1, "fixed": []}},
 "opt": {
  "Elemental Form": "Your Constitution rises by 2 and Wisdom by 1, to a maximum of 16 from this. You become an elemental in addition to your other types. Spells and effects that affect elementals of a specific CR do not affect you.",
  "Primordial Affinity": "One element sparked your birth. Choose it and gain its benefits. Air: Resistance to Lightning, and once on each of your turns you make a ranged weapon or ranged spell attack with Advantage (no effect without air currents, such as underwater). Earth: Resistance to Poison, and when you gain temporary hit points you gain your Proficiency Bonus more. Fire: Resistance to Fire, and you add your Constitution modifier to Fire damage you deal. Water: Resistance to Cold, and when a creature regains hit points from a spell or feature you control, it regains 1d6 plus your Constitution modifier more.",
  "Planar Binding (Primordial)": "Your body and soul are tied to a primordial plane. You have Disadvantage on death saves. If you would be killed, your soul returns to a plane the GM picks and you become an NPC there. On the primordial plane that caused your change, this Flaw does nothing.",
  "Call the Four": "As an action, call or push back the elements with one effect. Air: a 15-ft radius globe of breathable air around you that creatures can pass through but fire and water cannot, or one that banishes the air inside. It lasts 10 minutes and needs your concentration. Earth: conjure up to 50 lb of loose earth within 30 ft, or shape earth and stone within 15 ft, including making ground difficult terrain. Fire: ignite all loose flammable objects within 30 ft, or snuff all nonmagical flames within 30 ft. Water: conjure up to 10 gallons of water within 30 ft or make it rain in a 30-ft area, or repel water within 15 ft. This does not affect creatures but repels rain and mist and makes air pockets underwater.",
  "Dual Nature": "Add a second element from Primordial Affinity to your form and gain its benefits.",
  "Elemental Surge": "As an action choose one. Lightning Strike: a ranged attack on a creature within 60 ft, proficient, using Constitution, dealing 3d8 plus Constitution modifier Lightning damage. As a bonus action hit a second creature within 30 ft of the first. Earth Shard: a creature within 30 ft makes a Constitution save, taking 3d6 plus Constitution modifier Bludgeoning damage, or half on a success, and you gain temporary hit points equal to half. Flame Wave: each creature in a 15-ft cone from you makes a Dexterity save, taking 2d8 plus Constitution modifier Fire damage on a failure. Aquatic Rejuvenation: a creature you see within 60 ft regains 2d8 plus Constitution modifier hit points. Each effect rises by one die for each Transformation level above 2. You can use it a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier. A Long Rest restores all uses.",
  "Primordial: Hideous Appearance": "Your looks have twisted. You may have smoldering eyes, water pouring from your nose, sandy limbs or see-through skin. You can pass for the humanoid you were, but it takes concentration. You revert when you concentrate on a spell, fall unconscious or choose to. Under heavy stress the GM can call for a Constitution save with a DC they choose. Non-chaotic creatures that see your true form turn hostile unless the GM rules otherwise.",
  "Aura of Awakening": "You emit an aura that wakes elemental power in allies. Choose one when you gain it. You can change it after a Long Rest. You must be conscious. Light as Air: you and friendly creatures within 10 ft add your Constitution modifier to Dexterity saves. Forged in Fire: you and friendly creatures within 10 ft add your Constitution modifier as Fire damage to melee weapon hits. Heart of Stone: at the start of your turn, you and creatures you choose within 10 ft gain temporary hit points equal to your Constitution modifier. While they have them, and are not incapacitated, they cannot be moved or knocked prone unless they choose. Spring of Life: each unconscious creature of your choice within 10 ft regains 1 hit point at the start of its turn.",
  "Master of Many": "Requires Dual Nature. Add a third element from Primordial Affinity and gain its benefits as well.",
  "Primeval Body": "Your body is now fully elemental. You do not need to sleep, breathe or eat. You have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage from nonmagical attacks.",
  "Force of Nature": "You lose your link to society. After a Long Rest taken within civilization, you regain no Hit Dice and lose no exhaustion. The GM decides what counts as civilization, and may allow a park or grove in a city.",
  "Elemental Mastery": "Requires Master of Many. Add the fourth element and gain its benefits. You can also wreath yourself in all four elements. When a creature hits you with a melee attack, use your reaction to force a Dexterity save. It takes 8d6 Cold, Fire, Lightning or Bludgeoning damage (your choice), or half on a success. Until the end of your next turn your Primordial Affinity gains these. Air: Advantage on all ranged weapon and spell attacks. Earth: temporary hit points equal to your character level at the start of your turn. Fire: creatures of your choice within 5 ft take 2d6 Fire at the start of your turn. Water: healing you control restores your character level more hit points. You can use it a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier. A Long Rest restores all uses.",
  "Energy Flow": "As a bonus action, burst into elemental material and reappear up to 30 ft away in an open space you see, with your gear, without opportunity attacks. Then choose one. Swift Assault: make a weapon attack, with no Disadvantage on a ranged attack from a nearby hostile. Spark Storm: each creature within 10 ft makes a Dexterity save, taking 2d6 Fire damage on a failure. Boulderous Hide: choose a damage type and have Resistance to it until the start of your next turn. Sea Mother's Tether: link to a creature within 30 ft. While linked, either of you can choose to take damage meant for the other, and it cannot be reduced or prevented. You can use it a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier. A Long Rest restores all uses.",
  "Potent Aura": "Requires Aura of Awakening. Creatures of your choice within 10 ft have Resistance to Lightning, Fire, Poison and Cold damage.",
  "Pull of Chaos": "Your home plane tries to claim you. When you roll a natural 1 on a save against a spell or magical ability, you take 1d6 Force damage per two character levels on top of other effects. It ignores resistance and immunity."}},
"Specter": {"intro": _intro("Specter", "Your transformation comes from contact with the afterlife or a flaw in reality, as set at Spectral Presence."),
 "stages": {1: {"rule": "You gain Spectral Movement and Spectral Presence, and the Close to Death Flaw.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Spectral Movement", "Spectral Presence"]},
            2: {"rule": ONE, "take": 1, "fixed": []}, 3: {"rule": ONE, "take": 1, "fixed": []},
            4: {"rule": ONE + " Pull of Oblivion is a drawback. Take it if the GM asks.", "take": 1, "fixed": []}},
 "opt": {
  "Spectral Movement": "Your walking speed rises by 10 ft. You can move through creatures and solid objects as difficult terrain, and move through difficult terrain as normal. If you end your turn inside a creature or object, you return to where you entered and take 1d6 Force damage per 10 ft you traveled that way, rounded up. Items held less than 1 minute cannot pass through with you. On your turn you have Resistance to nonmagical Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage from sources you see.",
  "Spectral Presence": "Your Dexterity rises by 2 and Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 16 from this. If the cause is the afterlife, you become undead in addition to your other types. If it is a break in reality, you become an aberration in addition. Spells that affect humanoids still affect you, but you are immune to effects that only affect creatures of your new type of a specific CR. You stop aging and cannot be aged by magic.",
  "Close to Death": "Your hold on life is weak. You have Disadvantage on death saves. If you would be killed, the GM decides whether you die for good, beyond magical restoration, or become an incorporeal undead or aberration under GM control. On the Ethereal Plane this Flaw does nothing.",
  "Ethereal Phasing": "You can cast blink with no slot. After you do so a number of times equal to your Transformation level, you cannot again until a Long Rest.",
  "Horrifying Visage": "As an action, each creature of your choice within 30 ft that sees you makes a Wisdom save or is Frightened for 1 minute. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, with Disadvantage while you are in line of sight. You can use it a number of times equal to your Transformation level. A Long Rest restores all uses.",
  "Spectral Flight": "You gain a fly speed equal to your walking speed.",
  "Specter: Hideous Appearance": "Your true form is ghostly. It need not be scary, but it seems unnatural, and people may take you for a ghost or spirit. You can look like the humanoid you were with concentration. Heavy stress shows your true form: concentrating on a spell, falling unconscious, entering hallowed ground, or choosing to. The GM can call for a Constitution save with a DC they choose. How viewers react is the GM's call and may be hostile or fearful.",
  "Haunting Jaunt": "Requires Spectral Flight. As a bonus action, choose an open space within 120 ft and fly straight to it with no opportunity attacks. Each creature you pass through makes a Constitution save or takes 3d6 plus your Dexterity modifier Psychic damage and is Frightened of you until the end of your next turn. Short or Long Rest to use again.",
  "Life Drain": "As an action, a creature within 5 ft makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 8d8 Necrotic damage and you gain half that as temporary hit points. If it drops to 0, it dies and you regain one used charge of this Boon. You can use it a number of times equal to your Transformation level. A Long Rest restores all uses.",
  "Spectral Body": "You are immune to disease, exhaustion and Poison damage. When you take damage other than Force, use your reaction to gain Resistance to it and reveal your Hideous Appearance. You do not need air, food, water or sleep.",
  "Untethered Mind": "Your mind dissolves with your body. Memories of your life before the change fade like dreams. The GM can say you cannot recall something from your past when it is dramatic or costly. You have Disadvantage on Intelligence checks to recall information. Personality can shift, usually toward clinging to your old self or resenting those who live normally.",
  "Call of Unmaking": "As a bonus action, reveal your Hideous Appearance and wail. Constructs and undead are unaffected. Other creatures of your choice within 30 ft make a Constitution save, with Advantage if they cannot hear you. On a failure a creature bears the mark of unmaking for 1 minute and takes an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage whenever it takes damage. Long Rest to use again.",
  "Ethereal Denizen": "You sense invisible creatures and objects, and those on the nearby Ethereal Plane, as if under see invisibility. As an action you can cast etherealness with no slot. Short or Long Rest to use that again.",
  "Possession": "As an action, reveal your Hideous Appearance and enter the space of a humanoid or beast. It makes a Charisma save. On a failure you vanish, and the target is Incapacitated and you control its body while it stays aware. While possessing it you cannot be targeted by attacks, spells or other effects. You keep your alignment, Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma and immunity to Charmed and Frightened. Otherwise you use the target's statistics but not its knowledge, class features or proficiencies. It ends when the target drops to 0 hit points, you end it as a bonus action, or an effect forces you out. You then reappear within 5 ft of the body. Short or Long Rest to use again.",
  "Pull of Oblivion": "Nothingness pulls at you. When you roll a natural 1 on a save against an effect that deals damage, you lose 1d6 hit points per two levels. If you die, your body vanishes and only wish or true resurrection can raise you. If you and the GM agree, you may become an NPC monster, such as a wraith or a strange space-time aberration."}},
"Seraph": {"intro": _intro("Seraph", "You become a celestial chosen to embody a virtue."),
 "stages": {2: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Divine Protection"]},
            3: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Holy Bulwark"]},
            4: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Aura of Celestial Resilience"]}},
 "opt": {
  "Divine Protection": "When you or an ally you see within 30 ft is targeted by an attack, use your reaction to shield them with holy light. The target gets +4 AC against that attack. You can use it a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1). A Long Rest restores all uses.",
  "Holy Bulwark": "As an action, steel yourself against your hated foes and gain one benefit until you use this again. Stand Against the Infernal: Resistance to Fire damage. Cleanse the Undead: Resistance to Necrotic damage. Ignore Fey Trickery: immunity to Charmed and Frightened.",
  "Aura of Celestial Resilience": "You emit a 20-ft aura of firm conviction while you are conscious. When you or an ally in it fails a save, that creature can choose to succeed instead. Each creature can benefit once, then must finish a Long Rest."}},
"Lycanthrope": {"intro": _intro("Lycanthrope", "You carry a beast's curse. Your hybrid form lasts 1 hour per Transformation level."),
 "stages": {2: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Heart of the Wild"]},
            3: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level. It needs Hunter's Howl.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Call the Pack"]},
            4: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level. It needs Bestial Savagery.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Blood Frenzy"]}},
 "opt": {
  "Heart of the Wild": "Nature's spirits speak through your bestial side. You can cast and concentrate on spells in hybrid form. You can speak, read and write Sylvan, and have Advantage on Wisdom and Charisma checks to deal with fey and beasts.",
  "Call the Pack": "When you use Hunter's Howl, up to three allies you pick within 60 ft of the target gain its benefits too. It also gives them Advantage on attack rolls against the target if another affected ally within 5 ft of it is not incapacitated. When a hostile creature afflicted by your Hunter's Howl dies, you regain hit points equal to twice your Strength modifier.",
  "Blood Frenzy": "Your bite deals 2d8 damage. When you hit with it, the target makes a Strength save against your Transformation Save DC or is Grappled. While it is, you have Advantage on attacks against it and add your Strength modifier to damage with your natural weapons."}},
"Fiend": {"intro": _intro("Fiend", "You become a fiend through a bargain, a ritual or a cruel life. Gifts of Damnation come from the contracts you sign."),
 "stages": {2: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Brand of the Slaver's Flesh"]},
            3: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Infernal Sub-Contractor"]},
            4: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Loophole"]}},
 "opt": {
  "Brand of the Slaver's Flesh": "As an action, a flaming whip lashes a creature you see within 10 ft. It makes a Dexterity save against your Transformation Save DC. On a failure it takes 2d4 Fire damage and gets a searing brand, tying it to you by a leash of flame. It cannot move more than 10 ft from you by its own movement. On your turn, use a bonus action to drag it up to 10 ft in any direction. You can use your reaction to stop an event that would take it out of range, such as misty step or an ally dragging it away. Spells that teleport several creatures, such as dimension door, work for everyone except the branded one. The brand lasts 1 minute. It ends if the creature is knocked unconscious, enters hallowed ground, is hit by remove curse, or is more than 10 ft from you at the end of any turn.",
  "Infernal Sub-Contractor": "You can use the benefits of two Gifts of Damnation at once. You can change gifts after a Short Rest instead of a Long Rest.",
  "Loophole": "You know the workings of binding magic. You instantly know when a creature you meet was summoned. As an action, you can try to take control of a summoning spell from its caster. The caster makes a Wisdom save against your Transformation Save DC. On a failure you control the spell and its remaining creatures as if you cast it, including concentration for the rest of its duration. You can use it a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1). A Long Rest restores all uses."}},
"Lich": {"intro": _intro("Lich", "You bind part of your soul to a phylactery."),
 "stages": {2: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Phylactery Bond"]},
            3: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level. It needs Phylactery Bond.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Enhanced Phylactery"]},
            4: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level. It needs Enhanced Phylactery.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Soul Reflection"]}},
 "opt": {
  "Phylactery Bond": "You share a strong bond with your phylactery and benefit from keeping it on you. You can craft it into an amulet, ring, brooch or other jewelry. After a Short or Long Rest while wearing it, choose a damage type other than Radiant. While you wear it you are immune to that type. Your phylactery has AC 20 and 120 hit points. It is hidden from casual view, and an observer needs an Intelligence (Arcana) check against your Transformation Save DC to identify it.",
  "Enhanced Phylactery": "Your bond strengthens. If you wear no armor, your base AC is 15 plus your Dexterity modifier. Your phylactery's AC rises by 2. Your spell save DC and spell attack bonus each rise by 2. You and your phylactery have Advantage on saves against spells and other magical effects.",
  "Soul Reflection": "While wearing your phylactery, when a spell targets only you, use your reaction and spend phylactery charges equal to the spell's level to reflect it. It then targets an appropriate target you choose within its range, as if you cast it. Cantrips count as 1st level."}},
"Vampire": {"intro": _intro("Vampire", "You carry the Sanguine Curse."),
 "stages": {2: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Night Stalker"]},
            3: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level. It needs Shapechanger.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Improved Shapechanger"]},
            4: {"rule": "You gain the Boon of this Level. It needs Sanguine Magic.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Innate Sangromancy"]}},
 "opt": {
  "Night Stalker": "You gain proficiency in Stealth, or double your Proficiency Bonus if you have it. You can try to hide when only lightly obscured, including by dim light. You gain a climb speed equal to your walking speed and can climb difficult surfaces, even ceilings, without a check.",
  "Improved Shapechanger": "Your Shapechanger can also turn you into a dire wolf. In wolf form your speed is 50 ft. Sunlight hypersensitivity drops to sunlight sensitivity: in sunlight you have Disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks but take no damage from it. You cannot speak. Held items and worn armor merge into the form or fall, as the GM decides. You revert if you fall unconscious. You can use Fanged Bite in animal form, dealing 1 Piercing as a bat and 2d6 Piercing as a dire wolf. In mist form you can cast fog cloud once with no slot or components. Long Rest to use again.",
  "Innate Sangromancy": "You know all Sangromancy spells. When you cast one, you can pay with FP instead of Hit Dice, treating each FP as a d12. Casting this way earns no FP from Sanguine Magic. You can add one effect by paying more FP. Beguiling Spell (2 FP): a creature that fails its save is also Charmed until the end of your next turn. Shadow Spell (2 FP): a creature that fails cannot perceive you until the end of your next turn except by magic. Withering Spell (3 FP): a necrotic spell deals an extra 1d8 Necrotic per spell level, and a damaged creature cannot take reactions until the end of your next turn. Vampiric Spell (3 FP): a necrotic spell heals you for up to half the damage dealt."}},
}
